  "sentences": [
    {
      "text": "For our example, we have four strings, a hash B, an empty string, hello world, and the string containing 4 and 2.",
      "start_ms": 0,
      "end_ms": 9640,
      "start_frame": 0,
      "end_frame": 289,
      "word_count": 22
    },
    {
      "text": "Now suppose we simply join strings using a hash.",
      "start_ms": 10200,
      "end_ms": 13280,
      "start_frame": 306,
      "end_frame": 398,
      "word_count": 9
    },
    {
      "text": "Think about two different lists.",
      "start_ms": 14100,
      "end_ms": 15680,
      "start_frame": 423,
      "end_frame": 470,
      "word_count": 5
    },
    {
      "text": "One contains a hash B and C.",
      "start_ms": 16160,
      "end_ms": 19140,
      "start_frame": 485,
      "end_frame": 574,
      "word_count": 7
    },
    {
      "text": "The other contains a B and C.",
      "start_ms": 19480,
      "end_ms": 24100,
      "start_frame": 584,
      "end_frame": 723,
      "word_count": 7
    },
    {
      "text": "Both produce the same joint text, a hash B hash C.",
      "start_ms": 24540,
      "end_ms": 29400,
      "start_frame": 736,
      "end_frame": 882,
      "word_count": 11
    },
    {
      "text": "So how will the decoder know the original boundaries?",
      "start_ms": 30260,
      "end_ms": 33100,
      "start_frame": 908,
      "end_frame": 993,
      "word_count": 9
    },
    {
      "text": "It cannot?",
      "start_ms": 33860,
      "end_ms": 34460,
      "start_frame": 1016,
      "end_frame": 1034,
      "word_count": 2
    },
    {
      "text": "A raw separator is not enough.",
      "start_ms": 35680,
      "end_ms": 37680,
      "start_frame": 1070,
      "end_frame": 1130,
      "word_count": 6
    },
    {
      "text": "We need explicit boundary information.",
      "start_ms": 38260,
      "end_ms": 40800,
      "start_frame": 1148,
      "end_frame": 1224,
      "word_count": 5
    }
  ],
